Subject: [PATCH] Updated isntructions in readme, again

---
 README.md | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a41d741..10c6c09 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -203,8 +203,8 @@ Aurora is on SFP+ Port 0 (sfpp0). The AA target's defines are:
   On the X310 front panel, SFP0 is the left/top SFP+ cage (the one also used by the 1G/10G Ethernet configurations as the primary port). SFP1 carries the 1 GigE management/data link in this configuration.         
                                                           
   The X310's default IP addresses are stored in EEPROM (not in the FPGA bitfile), with factory defaults:                                                                                                             
-  - SFP0 (eth0): 192.168.10.2 (for Aurora on SFP1 use this for 1GigE)
-  - SFP1 (eth1): 192.168.20.2 (for Aurora on SFP0 use this for 1GigE)
+  - SFP0 (eth0): 192.168.10.2 **(for Aurora on SFP1 use this for 1GigE)**
+  - SFP1 (eth1): 192.168.20.2 **(for Aurora on SFP0 use this for 1GigE)**
                              
   In the X310_AA configuration SFP0 is aurora (bypasses Ethernet entirely), so the 1 GigE interface is on SFP1 at 192.168.20.2. The host NIC should be set to 192.168.20.1/24.                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
